  "body": "Part of #2526 (GPU shader toolpath generation). Slice 1 of 5.\n\nMaintainer order (2026-11-18): \"GPU shader issues get priority\". Thus this issue is `P4`.\n\n## Why\nThe ball drop-cutter of 3D finishing tests every facet for each sample. `support_at` (`crates/motion/src/finishing3d/support.rs` lines 368-388) loops over all `Sup` entries with a padded box reject only. Each accepted candidate calls `ball_clear` (lines 132-142), which loops over all facets again. `column_clear` (line 162) does the same. There is no spatial index. The cost is about samples x facets.\n\nThe GPU filter of #2526 must match a CPU reference. This slice makes that reference: a CPU grid of facets that the GPU result is tested against. It is also the largest speed gain (estimate in #2526, comment 3/4).\n\n## What\n- Bin the `Sup` entries (from `build_sups`, lines 27-50) into a uniform XY grid by their padded box (`xmin..xmax`, `ymin..ymax`, already padded by `r`).\n- `support_at`, `ball_clear`, `column_clear` and the fold scan (`edge.rs` `fold_best`) read only the facets of the cells that the query touches.\n- The same f64 functions run. The subset must hold every facet whose padded box contains the query point. This keeps the result the same bits.\n- Optional, same PR or a follow-up: run the raster lines in parallel with an order-preserving `collect`.\n- No GPU code in this slice.\n\n## Prime Directive\n- The grid is conservative: a facet goes into each cell that its padded box touches. A bin miss would let `ball_clear` pass a ball that touches a facet. A test pins the superset rule.\n- Degenerate input (NaN box, zero-area facet, a box past the coordinate guard) goes to every cell or gives a clean `GenError`. It never panics.\n\n## Pinning tests (CPU reference)\n- The 3D finishing goldens in `crates/app/tests/golden/` give the same `.cl` and `.cnc` bytes as before.\n- A new motion test: for random sample points over a fixture, the grid query answers the same `support_at` and `ball_clear` values as the full scan.\n- A new motion test: each facet whose padded box contains a point is in the grid query of that point (superset law).\n\n## Readings\nMeasure the time of one large 3D finishing operation before and after (release build). Put the numbers in the PR body.\n\n## Decision entry\nNot needed if the change stays inside `camcraft-motion`. No new crate edge, no new dependency.\n\nEffort: `effort:high` by the safety floor (toolpath generation and its gouge certifier).\n\nDone means: the 3D finishing support scan uses a facet grid, the goldens are byte-equal, the superset and parity tests pass, and the PR states the speed readings.\n",
